  <h1>Tiro Finance Sync — Terms</h1>
  <p class="caption">terms of use for a personal, non-commercial banking sync</p>

  <p>
    Tiro Finance Sync is a personal tool built and operated by Davide Pucci
    for his own use only. by using it (which, in practice, only he does),
    the following applies.
  </p>

  <h2>purpose</h2>
  <p>
    the tool synchronizes the operator's own bank accounts into his own
    budgeting software via the Enable Banking API, using read-only access
    granted through the bank's authentication with explicit consent.
  </p>

  <h2>no service offered</h2>
  <p>
    nothing here is offered to the public. there is no account to create,
    no subscription, no support channel and no service-level commitment.
  </p>

  <h2>acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    access credentials, API sessions and synced data belong to the operator
    and must not be shared or repurposed. bank consent sessions expire and
    must be renewed through the bank's own login — never by sharing banking
    credentials with anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>as-is</h2>
  <p>
    the tool is provided as-is, without warranties of any kind. categorization
    and reports are best-effort personal bookkeeping, not financial advice.
  </p>

